WEBVTT

00:01.280 --> 00:06.720
JGBT is no longer just the AI chatbot that everyone has heard of, it's really becoming

00:06.720 --> 00:12.860
an operating system for how leaders write, research, analyze, automate and get all of

00:12.860 --> 00:14.120
their work done.

00:14.580 --> 00:20.380
And with close to a billion weekly users, OpenAI's flagship assistant now combines powerful

00:20.380 --> 00:23.900
models with an incredible amount of features.

00:24.100 --> 00:25.740
So let's take a look at those features.

00:25.740 --> 00:29.500
First of all, there's Surge, which pulls live web answers.

00:30.060 --> 00:35.520
And there's also Deep Research, which synthesizes many sources into a structured sighted report.

00:36.120 --> 00:41.560
There's file uploads, vision and data analysis, so you can drop in PDFs, spreadsheets, images

00:41.560 --> 00:44.560
or charts and then JGBT will analyze them for you.

00:45.080 --> 00:50.780
Voice lets you talk naturally to JGBT and paid plans even at real-time video and screen

00:50.780 --> 00:52.140
sharing on mobile.

00:52.620 --> 00:55.740
The newly launched Images 2.0 is amazing.

00:56.000 --> 01:01.820
It generates visuals like mock-ups, diagrams and posters with better text layout and instruction

01:01.820 --> 01:02.320
following.

01:02.880 --> 01:08.080
Canvas is a dedicated workspace for writing and coding rather than managing long projects

01:08.080 --> 01:09.020
in a chat thread.

01:09.880 --> 01:15.440
Projects organize your chats, your files and instructions around ongoing work, while custom

01:15.440 --> 01:19.060
JGBTs let you build reusable task-specific assistants.

01:19.740 --> 01:25.160
Apps connect external tools like drives like GitHub, HubSpot and Asana so that JGBT can

01:25.160 --> 01:31.180
answer from your private work context and skills package repeatable workflows with instructions,

01:31.620 --> 01:35.760
example and codes for more consistent task execution.

01:36.600 --> 01:41.880
Tasks handle scheduled lightweight automation work like reminders, recurring briefings and

01:41.880 --> 01:42.780
future follow-ups.

01:43.060 --> 01:48.640
And JGBT agent can autonomously browse the web for you, navigate pages, fill forms and

01:48.640 --> 01:49.700
edit spreadsheets.

01:50.320 --> 01:56.120
Memory, custom instructions and tone let JGBT learn your preferences and adapt its behavior

01:56.120 --> 02:01.100
over time and then there's Codex which is OpenAI's coding agent for writing, reviewing,

02:01.420 --> 02:02.880
debugging and shipping code.

02:04.380 --> 02:05.540
Now those are the features.

02:05.720 --> 02:08.380
What about the models that power this platform?

02:08.740 --> 02:11.420
Well, the models are best understood in three layers.

02:11.680 --> 02:13.820
Instant, Thinking and Pro.

02:13.820 --> 02:20.380
So, JGBT 5.3 Instant is the current fast everyday model which is designed for normal questions,

02:20.740 --> 02:24.280
for writing, for summarizing, for brainstorming and any kind of quick work.

02:24.760 --> 02:32.280
But launched on April 23rd, JGBT 5.5 Thinking is the main model for serious professional work.

02:32.400 --> 02:33.880
This is the one that we always use.

02:34.460 --> 02:39.560
OpenAI calls it the smartest and most intuitive to use model yet and the strengths really are in

02:39.560 --> 02:44.760
coding and online research, in data analysis, in document and spreadsheet creation,

02:45.200 --> 02:48.300
tool use and even in operating software.

02:48.760 --> 02:54.500
And then there is JGBT 5.5 Pro which is a research grade model for your hardest questions

02:54.500 --> 02:56.720
and your highest accuracy work.

02:56.860 --> 03:01.000
So, you can really use this for tasks that need deeper reasoning, stronger structure

03:01.000 --> 03:03.500
and more confidence in the final answer.

03:04.520 --> 03:09.740
Now, in terms of privacy and data use, for personal plans, training and data sharing settings

03:09.740 --> 03:11.480
can be adjusted in settings.

03:12.000 --> 03:16.460
But for business, enterprise and education plans, OpenAI says that organizational data

03:16.460 --> 03:19.000
is not used for training by default.

03:19.560 --> 03:24.720
Then on May 1, JGBT also rolled out advanced account security which then adds stronger

03:24.720 --> 03:29.680
sign in protection like pass keys or security keys and strict recovery checks.

03:29.680 --> 03:35.140
Of course, regardless of any plan, avoid sharing sensitive information that you wouldn't share

03:35.140 --> 03:38.940
with a third party vendor and verify any outputs that matter.

03:39.840 --> 03:45.160
And finally, in terms of plans and pricing, JGBT now offers a pretty wide range of pricing

03:45.160 --> 03:45.620
models.

03:45.840 --> 03:51.900
There's free for everyday use with 10 messages on JGBT 5.3 every 5 hours and then after that

03:51.900 --> 03:53.520
you fall back to 5.3 mini.

03:53.700 --> 03:56.220
You can also get a couple of tools but with pretty tight limits.

03:56.220 --> 04:01.760
There's Go which is $8 per month which gives you slightly higher limits than free plus a

04:01.760 --> 04:05.920
larger context window but most of us should be using plus.

04:06.140 --> 04:11.600
20 bucks per month, higher 5.5 thinking limits, you have faster responses, you also get voice,

04:11.780 --> 04:15.360
you get image generation, you get file uploads and analysis, you get deep research,

04:15.820 --> 04:19.120
custom JGBT creation and use and even codecs.

04:19.680 --> 04:23.320
Now, if you run into usage limits there then you have to switch to Pro which is between

04:23.320 --> 04:29.700
100 and 200 bucks per month which also includes access to 5.5 pro and then there's the business

04:29.700 --> 04:35.420
and enterprise plans which adds access and then there's the business and enterprise plans which

04:35.420 --> 04:42.160
also adds admin controls, governance, share projects, company knowledge, agents and permissions and

04:42.160 --> 04:45.900
these plans start around $25 per user per month.

04:46.700 --> 04:51.780
But in short, JGBT now really covers more of the senior work that you would do than any

04:51.780 --> 04:53.140
single tool before it.

